From skeid #29 review I2 (general path): with a config_loader, maybe_reload_config runs on every call_function (every chat request); each run rebuilds the node list, which bumps the inventory generation and restarts probes. Fix: loader-based reload needs a change detector (loader returns a version/etag/digest, or skeid digests the loaded structure) and a throttle; identical node lists must not reset probes; keep admin-API-set health across a no-op reload. Tests counting loader calls/probe restarts over N requests.
